            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.9 (build 807)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Kitsu sign-in works again.</b> A per-user sign-in lasts a week; when yours ran out, Asobi kept using the dead token &#8212; every request came back &#8220;token rejected&#8221; while the panel still said you were signed in, and signing in again silently failed to replace it. Now an expired sign-in is ignored (the studio account carries on where it can), the panel tells you the date yours ran out, and a sign-in that can&#8217;t be saved says so instead of claiming success.</li>
<li>The manual&#8217;s Web Review chapter has figures for the first time &#8212; the orange Shots pill, the labelled toolbar, the tools panel, &#8220;What&#8217;s where&#8221; and the phone layout &#8212; and the cheat-sheet and transport figures are current.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
